  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1145 PM CDT THU SEP 3 2026\n\nStout upper-level ridging will remain in the driver's seat for\nthe majority of this forecast period, with no real end in sight.\nThere will be some slight relief this weekend, as the apex of the\nridge breaks down and shifts west, allowing a disturbance along\nthe Gulf to slide north. Unfortunately, this relief is limited,\nwith the best rain chances this weekend remaining along the I-\n85 corridor. Isolated and scattered rain chances will also remain\nin the forecast through the middle of the week, with the center\nof the ridge remaining over the central Plains, but widespread\nrainfall is not expected.\n\nBy the middle of next week, a deep trough will begin to take\nshape over the west coast, shifting the ridge right back over top\nof us. High temperatures will quickly rebound, climbing right\nback into the mid and upper-90s. However, given some uncertainty\nin afternoon dewpoint values, confidence in the need for\nadditional heat headlines during this time is low. Regardless, it\ndoes appear that the heat is here to stay.\n\n/44/",
